Mon Jul 06 2026  emarti, Murat Ozdemir

	* Rewrote showbord.c board rendering:
	  - Unified single 19x19 loop (was 7 separate sections), 323→106 lines
	  - ASCII edge/corner characters: top=& bottom=* left=, right=(
	  - Corners: % (top-left), ' (top-right), + (bottom-left), ) (bottom-right)
	  - Empty board positions: ! (was PETSCII $7B)
	  - Star points: - (was +)
	  - Stone display: WHITE=$ BLACK=# (was O/X)
	  - Board rendering color 0x09 (light blue), default 0x0F (light gray)
	  - Color RAM for empty positions uses 0x09 (was 0x0F)
	  - Case-swapped all printf strings for C64 lowercase PETSCII mode
	  - Status line: removed comma between You/Computer scores
	  - "Computer move:" on separate line below score

	* Fixed scoring bug in exambord.c:
	  - ++mk/++uk were swapped; user captures now correctly increment uk,
	    computer captures increment mk

	* Updated main.c:
	  - "Thinking..." printed before genmove() during computer's turn
	  - pass/stop input now case-insensitive (accepts both "pass" and "PASS")
	  - After game end, jmp $fce2 warm reset to return to C64 BASIC
	  - Case-swapped all printf strings for PETSCII lowercase mode
	  - "computer move:" promoted to own line, comma removed from score line

	* Updated getmove.c:
	  - pass/stop comparison case-insensitive

	* Added .gitignore for build artifacts (*.asm, *.int, *.lbl, *.map, *.prg)

	* Updated Makefile: added clean target

Sun Jul 05 2026  emarti, Murat Ozdemir

	* Ported to C64 using oscar64 compiler with -Os flag for minimal PRG size
	
	* Added fontdata.c - custom font initialization for C64 PETSCII graphics
	
	* Updated main.c:
	  - Added c64/memmap.h include and fontinit() extern
	  - Added #pragma region/stacksize/heapsize for memory layout
	  - Replaced argc/argv with void signature
	  - Added C64 screen initialization (CHR$ codes, PETSCII mode)
	  - Disabled showinst(), save/restore game, and handicap prompts
	  - Removed handicap selection (always 0 for C64)
	  - Used clock() instead of time() for random seed
	
	* Updated gnugo.h: commented out showinst() declaration (disabled for C64)
	
	* Updated showinst.c: wrapped entire function in comment block (disabled)
	
	* Updated showbord.c: replaced spaced board display with compact version
	  to fit C64 40-column screen; side info uses compact labels (U:W, C:B, etc.)
	
	* Updated getmove.c: disabled save command (FILE I/O not practical on C64)
	
	* Updated count.c: converted from recursive to iterative (stack-based)
	  to reduce C64 stack pressure; added CSTACK_MAX/cstack/csp
	
	* Updated findnext.c: converted from recursive to iterative (stack-based);
	  made fval static; added fstack/fsp
	
	* Updated findopen.c: converted from recursive to iterative (stack-based);
	  added OSTACK_MAX/ostack/osp
	
	* Updated endgame.c: moved mymovelist/umovelist from local to static
	  file-scope arrays to reduce stack usage
	
	* Updated Makefile: added fontdata.c to SRC; added C64 target (make c64)
	  building gnugo.prg via oscar64 -Os
	
	* Fixed oscar64 compiler warnings:
	  - matchpat.c: initialized ti/tj to 0 (uninitialized variable)
	  - findcolr.c: initialized result to 0 (uninitialized variable)
	  - endgame.c: replaced 2D array p[][] with flat pointer pp in
	    createlist to avoid "Undefined constant pointer arithmetic"
	    and inlined node() macro as i*BSIZE+j

